# InTell: Cursor rules

**Before any task, read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root in full.** It holds the workflow, repo layout, conventions and open decisions. For the mobile app, also read `apps/mobile/AGENTS.md`. If a brief exists in `docs/briefs/` for your task, follow its scope exactly.

The non-negotiables (full text in AGENTS.md §5; ADR 0004 beats older spec text):
1. The place comes first: the core experience is being on site. Map home with Chronicle (bottom left), Journal (bottom right), a center button (TBD) and Settings (top right). No feeds, search, nearby lists, gamification or push notifications.
2. No AI-generated text, narration, music or sound. Replaceplace staff produce everything that plays.
3. In situ first: fragments are first heard only on site (proximity, physical-marker scan, accessible play within 35 ft) and are replayable in the Chronicle only after completion on site, per Day/Night version.
4. Locked fragments show at 35% with their teaser only; never their title, transcript or audio. Marker codes never leave Postgres.
5. Location never leaves the device; "While Using" permission only.
6. Play only what's in the current pack manifests; sync deletes everything else. Content reaches phones only through published releases.
7. No secrets or service role key in client code (mobile or admin); `device_id` is secret.
8. Age gate and PII stripping for Journal entries; entries are private to staff.
9. Transcripts, accessibility labels, alt text, i18n, reduced motion, feet and miles, always.

Plan before coding, list spec ambiguities, one milestone per branch, and keep `pnpm lint && pnpm typecheck && pnpm test` green. Don't build past a *Proposed* ADR (audio engine: ADR 0001) or an open question in ADR 0004.
